  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Swap places and go at goal",
  "description": "Two attackers against two defenders towards a goal with a keeper, starting about 30 metres out. Behind the attackers stand two support players with the balls. They play the ball in and can be used for passes back, but don't join the attack themselves.\n\nThe attackers move a lot and swap places with each other – for example with crossing runs – to lose their defender and get free at goal. The defenders are moderately active at first. An attempt ends with a goal, when the defenders win the ball or when it goes out. After a few attempts, the pairs rotate: attackers become supporters, supporters become defenders and defenders become attackers.\n\nVariation: fully active defenders, and compete pair against pair. A goal scores a point for both the attackers and the support players. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Swap places at speed – one run takes a defender away and opens space for the other."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Use the support players: pass back rather than lose the ball in a crowd."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Cross your runs and call, so you don't both run into the same space."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Support players: play the ball in at the right moment, in front of the runner."
    }
  ],
